@startuml
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam ArrowColor #40546E
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #F5F7FB
skinparam maxMessageSize 250
hide footbox
title Strategy in use | Practice words: choose a method and 11 words

actor Student
participant ConsoleClient as Console
participant LanguageLearningFacade as Facade
participant ReviewClient as Client
participant ReviewContext as Context
participant "chosenStrategy: ReviewStrategy" as Strategy

Student -> Console : Practice words; method; count = 11; exercise mode
note over Console, Strategy
  Choice 1: SpacedRepetitionStrategy.
  Choice 2: WeakWordsStrategy.
end note
Console -> Facade : startReview(chosenStrategy, 11, mode)
Facade -> Client : selectForPractice(strategy, vocabulary, progress, 11, today)
activate Client
Client -> Client : select(strategy, vocabulary, progress, 11, today)
Client -> Context : setStrategy(chosenStrategy)
Client -> Context : select(vocabulary, progress, 11, today)
Context -> Strategy : select(vocabulary, progress, 11, today)
note right of Strategy
  Spaced repetition: studied and due words first.
  Weak words: studied words with lowest accuracy first.
end note
Strategy --> Context : priority words (up to 11)
Context --> Client : immutable priority list
note over Client
  Inline fill step in selectForPractice():
  keep priorities in a LinkedHashSet;
  append unselected new words, then other words;
  stop at exactly 11 distinct words.
end note
Client --> Facade : immutable list of 11 words
deactivate Client
note over Facade
  Build practice exercises from these words
  through LessonBuilderClient and create LessonSession.
end note
Facade --> Console : LessonSession containing 11 exercises
Console --> Student : 11 practice questions

note over Facade, Client
  The separate dueCount() operation uses select() with the due strategy.
  Its result counts truly due words; filling practice does not alter that count.
end note
@enduml
